00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:14,520
She wants to take Kenny to the park and get some fresh air.

102
00:06:15,220 --> 00:06:17,800
Now, what does it mean to go get fresh air?

103
00:06:18,240 --> 00:06:26,220
Well, basically, it means to go out and maybe walk or just be outside and get air from the outside.

104
00:06:26,560 --> 00:06:29,500
Because sometimes you're in your house all the time, and that's not fresh air.

105
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:30,340
That's right.

106
00:06:30,480 --> 00:06:33,160
So basically, this means exactly what you're saying. It means going outside.

107
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:38,000
So kids often need to go get some fresh air, but also adults do, too.

108
00:06:38,060 --> 00:06:43,040
Sometimes I feel like when I'm working in the office for a long time, I really need to get some fresh air.

109
00:06:43,540 --> 00:06:45,380
So that means I go outside for a walk.

110
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:45,800
Exactly.

111
00:06:46,460 --> 00:06:49,880
And you can tell your friends, oh, excuse me for a minute.

112
00:06:50,020 --> 00:06:51,460
I'm going to go get some fresh air.

113
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,380
Or you know what? You're looking a little bit pale.

114
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:55,280
Maybe you should go get some fresh air.

115
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:56,320
Exactly.

116
